IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `lpul-practice`
IMPORT `lpul-trust`
IMPORT `lpul-costs`

-- Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) -- the questions people ask, for two seats in one layer (the Q&A layer).
--
-- ROLES. The seat is a parameter: every exported question takes `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). The
-- roles are the two people the Uniform Law puts duties on or gives rights to who would ask it questions:
--   - the lawyer: admitted to the Australian legal profession, practising or about to (the baseline's seat, Daniel in
--     the WA lives). The duties of the law practice are met by its lawyers, so the firm's duties are asked as his;
--   - the client of a law practice: the person whose money the firm holds and who is billed (Parts 4.2 and 4.3 give the
--     client its rights: trust money, costs disclosure, bills, assessment).
-- A question about the other role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input. The Legal Practice
-- Board, costs assessors and the designated tribunal are never seats: what they may or must do appears as an input
-- (their judgment, answered conditionally) or as what it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the graffiti encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that
-- situation's fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it does not hold, without
-- reading anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, character for character, across both roles:
--   - `I hold a current practising certificate` (the lawyer): the conditions of a certificate (ss 47, 48(2), 50, 51, 54,
--     88) bind only "the holder". FALSE gives does not arise. It is also an ordinary input of three questions that arise
--     whether or not I hold one (qualified entity, holding out, solicitor or barrister);
--   - `the law practice holds money for the client` (both roles): Part 4.2 and General Rules rr 42, 52 arise only for
--     money the practice has received or holds. FALSE gives does not arise;
--   - `the bill given` (both roles): the s 187 questions arise only after a lump sum bill (s 187(1)); suing, interest
--     and the s 207 conduct question only after a bill. `no bill has been given yet` gives does not arise, except for
--     "May my firm sue" and its client mirror, which keep the baseline's answer no (no bill, s 194(1)) and read nothing
--     else (as the graffiti layer's D8.1 keeps a no that settles the question);
--   - `the costs have been assessed` (both roles): who pays the costs of an assessment (s 204). FALSE gives does not
--     arise.
-- A question that arises in every situation of its role takes no situation input.
--
-- CONTENT. For the lawyer, every exported question of the baseline (lpul-practice.l4, lpul-trust.l4, lpul-costs.l4) is
-- asked by calling its function; where the baseline takes a record (the money, the withdrawal, the bill, the offence,
-- the disclosure, the interest claim, the ledger), this layer takes each of its fields as a plain input and builds the
-- record, so the form can ask them one by one. The baseline's "I am an Australian lawyer" is TRUE by the lawyer's role
-- (admitted). For the client, the questions are the same rules asked from the other side, by the same functions, plus
-- three this layer adds from the text: the last day for the itemised bill (s 187(3)), the last day to apply for
-- assessment (s 198(3)) and whether the person acting for me is a qualified entity (s 6). Inputs shared by both roles
-- are worded of "the client" and "the law practice", so one wording serves both.
--
-- No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input. Edition, scope and findings: NOTES.md.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to`
    `I am the client of a law practice`

-- s 186: "A bill may be in the form of a lump sum bill or an itemised bill." The bill situation.
DECLARE `The bill given` IS ONE OF
    `no bill has been given yet`
    `a lump sum bill`
    `an itemised bill, with no lump sum bill before it`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Penalty` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `up to` HAS `penalty units` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Rate` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `at most` HAS `percent a year` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Date answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

DECLARE `Holding out` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `on holding out` HAS `holding out answer` IS A `Holding out answer`

DECLARE `Firm holding out` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `on my firm` HAS `firm holding out answer` IS A `Firm holding out answer`

DECLARE `Branch` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `I am` HAS `branch` IS A `Branch of the profession`

DECLARE `Reporting` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `on reporting` HAS `reporting answer` IS A `Reporting answer`

DECLARE `Where it goes` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the money goes` HAS `where the money goes` IS A `Where the money goes`

DECLARE `Withdrawal` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `on the withdrawal` HAS `withdrawal answer` IS A `Withdrawal answer`

DECLARE `Disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `disclosure due` HAS `disclosure answer` IS A `Disclosure answer`

DECLARE `Further disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `further disclosure due` HAS `further disclosure answer` IS A `Further disclosure answer`

DECLARE `Non-disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `what follows` HAS `non-disclosure answer` IS A `Non-disclosure answer`

DECLARE `Suing` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `on suing` HAS `suing answer` IS A `Suing answer`

DECLARE `Assessment` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `on assessment` HAS `assessment answer` IS A `Assessment answer`

DECLARE `Assessment costs` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the assessment costs` HAS `assessment costs answer` IS A `Assessment costs answer`

§§ `Building the baseline's inputs`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The situation helpers list every value and have no OTHERWISE: on the stable l4 a CONSIDER with OTHERWISE takes the
-- OTHERWISE branch for an ASSUMEd value instead of failing (graffiti finding 31), so the cases could not show the
-- situation is read first.
GIVEN `the bill given` IS A `The bill given`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no bill has been given` IF
    CONSIDER `the bill given`
    WHEN `no bill has been given yet` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a lump sum bill` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an itemised bill, with no lump sum bill before it` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the bill given` IS A `The bill given`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no lump sum bill has been given` IF
    CONSIDER `the bill given`
    WHEN `no bill has been given yet` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a lump sum bill` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an itemised bill, with no lump sum bill before it` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `the offence's class` IS AN `Offence class`
      `the offence is under transport or traffic legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is about parking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is about driving or operating a vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was sentenced to imprisonment for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its maximum imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
      `a licence disqualification was ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was drink or drug driving under the NSW or Victorian Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The offence`
`the offence built from` MEANS
    `The offence` WITH
        `class` IS `the offence's class`
        `under transport or traffic legislation` IS `the offence is under transport or traffic legislation`
        `about parking` IS `the offence is about parking`
        `about driving or operating a vehicle` IS `the offence is about driving or operating a vehicle`
        `I was sentenced to imprisonment` IS `I was sentenced to imprisonment for it`
        `maximum imprisonment in months` IS `its maximum imprisonment in months`
        `licence disqualification ordered` IS `a licence disqualification was ordered`
        `drink or drug driving under the NSW or Victorian Act` IS `it was drink or drug driving under the NSW or Victorian Act`

GIVEN `what the money is` IS A `What the money is`
      `it was received at the client's direction in the ordinary course of legal practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Board has determined it is not trust money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Uniform Rules declare it is not trust money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was received in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a written direction to deal with it otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The money`
`the money built from` MEANS
    `The money` WITH
        `what it is` IS `what the money is`
        `received in the ordinary course of legal practice at the client's direction` IS `it was received at the client's direction in the ordinary course of legal practice`
        `invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value` IS `it is invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value`
        `determined under s 152 not to be trust money` IS `the Board has determined it is not trust money`
        `declared by the Uniform Rules not to be trust money` IS `the Uniform Rules declare it is not trust money`
        `received in cash` IS `it was received in cash`
        `a written direction to deal with it otherwise` IS `there is a written direction to deal with it otherwise`

GIVEN `a bill referring to the withdrawal was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the bill was given` IS A DATE
      `business days since the bill was given` IS A NUMBER
      `the client objected within 7 business days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the client referred it to the Board or for costs assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the client asked for and received an itemised bill` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the itemised bill was received` IS A DATE
      `the money has otherwise become legally payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the client's instructions authorise the withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it reimburses money the law practice paid for the client` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the client was first sent a request for payment or notice of withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My withdrawal`
`the withdrawal built from` MEANS
    `My withdrawal` WITH
        `I gave a bill referring to the proposed withdrawal` IS `a bill referring to the withdrawal was given`
        `the date the bill was given` IS `the day the bill was given`
        `business days since the bill was given` IS `business days since the bill was given`
        `the client objected within 7 business days` IS `the client objected within 7 business days`
        `the client referred it to the Board or for costs assessment` IS `the client referred it to the Board or for costs assessment`
        `the client asked for and received an itemised bill` IS `the client asked for and received an itemised bill`
        `the date the itemised bill was received` IS `the day the itemised bill was received`
        `the money has otherwise become legally payable` IS `the money has otherwise become legally payable`
        `the client's instructions authorise the withdrawal` IS `the client's instructions authorise the withdrawal`
        `it reimburses money my firm paid for the client` IS `it reimburses money the law practice paid for the client`
        `I first sent a request for payment or notice of withdrawal` IS `the client was first sent a request for payment or notice of withdrawal`

GIVEN `the ledger has only transit money or written direction money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the balance at 30 June was zero` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there was no transaction in the 12 months before 30 June` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement was given in those 12 months and there has been no transaction since` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My client's trust ledger`
`the ledger built from` MEANS
    `My client's trust ledger` WITH
        `only transit money or written direction money` IS `the ledger has only transit money or written direction money`
        `the balance at 30 June was zero` IS `the balance at 30 June was zero`
        `no transaction in the 12 months before 30 June` IS `there was no transaction in the 12 months before 30 June`
        `a statement was given in those 12 months and no transaction since` IS `a statement was given in those 12 months and there has been no transaction since`

-- The s 194 bill: with no bill given, the record says no complying bill was given, and the baseline answers no on that
-- field alone (its first test), reading no other.
GIVEN `the bill given` IS A `The bill given`
      `the bill complies with the Law and the Uniform Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the bill was given` IS A DATE
      `the client asked for and received an itemised bill` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the itemised bill was received` IS A DATE
      `a costs dispute before the Board is unresolved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a costs assessment is applied for and not complete` IS A BOOLEAN
      `disclosure failed and the costs are not yet assessed or determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My unpaid bill`
`the unpaid bill built from` MEANS
    `My unpaid bill` WITH
        `a bill complying with the Law and the Rules was given` IS
            IF `no bill has been given` `the bill given` THEN FALSE ELSE `the bill complies with the Law and the Uniform Rules`
        `the date the bill was given` IS `the day the bill was given`
        `the client received an itemised bill after asking under s 187` IS `the client asked for and received an itemised bill`
        `the date the itemised bill was received` IS `the day the itemised bill was received`
        `a costs dispute before the Board is unresolved` IS `a costs dispute before the Board is unresolved`
        `a costs assessment is applied for and not complete` IS `a costs assessment is applied for and not complete`
        `disclosure failed and the costs are not yet assessed or determined` IS `disclosure failed and the costs are not yet assessed or determined`

GIVEN `a costs agreement provides for interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days the costs have been unpaid since the bill` IS A NUMBER
      `the bill states that interest is payable and the rate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rate charged` IS A NUMBER
      `the Cash Rate Target when the bill was issued` IS A NUMBER
      `the bill was given more than 6 months after the matter was completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lateness came from the client's request or a late itemised bill request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My interest claim`
`the interest claim built from` MEANS
    `My interest claim` WITH
        `a costs agreement provides for interest` IS `a costs agreement provides for interest`
        `days the costs have been unpaid since the bill` IS `days the costs have been unpaid since the bill`
        `the bill states that interest is payable and the rate` IS `the bill states that interest is payable and the rate`
        `the rate charged` IS `the rate charged`
        `the Cash Rate Target when the bill was issued` IS `the Cash Rate Target when the bill was issued`
        `the bill was given more than 6 months after the matter was completed` IS `the bill was given more than 6 months after the matter was completed`
        `the lateness came from the client's request or a late itemised bill request` IS `the lateness came from the client's request or a late itemised bill request`

§§ `For the lawyer`

§§§ `Holding out (ss 6, 11, 12)`

-- The lawyer's role is admitted, so the baseline's "I am an Australian lawyer" is TRUE by the role's own terms.
@export Am I a qualified entity under the Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) s 6?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a current practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a current Australian practising certificate
      `another law authorises my legal practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a law of the Commonwealth or a State, other than the Uniform Law, authorises you to engage in legal practice
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I a qualified entity, as a lawyer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        `yes if` (`Am I a qualified entity` TRUE `I hold a current practising certificate` `another law authorises my legal practice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I presumed to have represented that I am entitled to engage in legal practice (Uniform Law s 12(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I used a title listed in s 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you took or used a title such as lawyer, solicitor, barrister, counsel or legal practitioner
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I presumed to have represented that I may practise` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        `yes if` (`Am I presumed to have represented that I am entitled to practise` `I used a title listed in s 12(1)`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I advertise, represent or imply that I am entitled to engage in legal practice (Uniform Law s 11(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a current practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a current Australian practising certificate
      `another law authorises my legal practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a law of the Commonwealth or a State, other than the Uniform Law, authorises you to engage in legal practice
GIVETH A `Holding out`
`May I say I may practise` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        `on holding out` (`May I say I am entitled to engage in legal practice` TRUE `I hold a current practising certificate` `another law authorises my legal practice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I, as an employee, partner or agent, represent that my firm is entitled to engage in legal practice (Uniform Law s 11(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the entity is a law practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is a law practice (for example a law firm of Australian legal practitioners)
      `the entity is otherwise a qualified entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is otherwise a qualified entity under s 6
GIVETH A `Firm holding out`
`May I say my firm may practise` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        `on my firm` (`May I say my firm is entitled to engage in legal practice` `the entity is a law practice` `the entity is otherwise a qualified entity`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `My practising certificate (ss 6, 47, 48, 50, 51, 54, 88, 150)`

-- Arises with or without a certificate: without one the answer is "neither", as in the baseline, and the category is
-- not read.
@export Am I a solicitor or a barrister under the Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) s 6?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a current practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a current Australian practising certificate
      `my certificate's category` IS A `Category of practice` @desc The category of practice your certificate authorises
GIVETH A `Branch`
`Am I a solicitor or a barrister, as a lawyer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        `I am` (`Am I a solicitor or a barrister` `I hold a current practising certificate` `my certificate's category`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my practising certificate let me practise in this capacity (Uniform Law s 47(1), (3)-(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a current practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a current Australian practising certificate
      `my certificate's category` IS A `Category of practice` @desc The category of practice your certificate authorises
      `the capacity I want to practise in` IS A `Category of practice` @desc The capacity you want to practise in
      `my certificate has been renewed since that category was determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your certificate has been renewed since (s 47(4) lasts only until renewal)
      `a discretionary condition restricts my pro bono work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a s 53 discretionary condition prohibits or restricts your pro bono or community legal service work
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my certificate let me practise in this capacity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF NOT `I hold a current practising certificate`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does my certificate let me practise as` `my certificate's category` `the capacity I want to practise in` `my certificate has been renewed since that category was determined` `a discretionary condition restricts my pro bono work`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The firm's authority turns on a principal's certificate, not mine (s 150), so it arises whether or not I hold one.
@export May my firm receive trust money (Uniform Law s 150, General Rules r 56)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a principal holds a certificate authorising receipt of trust money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a principal (for example a partner) of the law practice holds a practising certificate authorising the receipt of trust money
      `the firm is otherwise authorised under the Uniform Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice is otherwise authorised under the Uniform Rules (General Rules r 56)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my firm receive trust money, as a lawyer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        `yes if` (`May my firm receive trust money` `a principal holds a certificate authorising receipt of trust money` `the firm is otherwise authorised under the Uniform Rules`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I apply for another practising certificate (Uniform Law s 48(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a current practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a current Australian practising certificate
      `it would be in force at the same time as my current certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the new certificate would be in force at the same time as the one you hold
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I apply for another certificate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF NOT `I hold a current practising certificate`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I apply for another practising certificate` `it would be in force at the same time as my current certificate`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I complete a barrister's reading program (Uniform Law s 50)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a current practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a current Australian practising certificate
      `my certificate's category` IS A `Category of practice` @desc The category of practice your certificate authorises
      `I have satisfied the reading condition before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already completed the reading program and reading period
      `the Board directs me to do it again` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has directed you to comply again
      `the Board has exempted me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has exempted you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I do a reading program` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF NOT `I hold a current practising certificate`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must I complete a reading program` `my certificate's category` `I have satisfied the reading condition before` `the Board directs me to do it again` `the Board has exempted me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I report this to the Legal Practice Board, and how (Uniform Law ss 51, 86, 88, General Rules r 15)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a current practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a current Australian practising certificate
      `what happened` IS A `What happened` @desc What happened to you
      `the offence's class` IS AN `Offence class` @desc For a charge or conviction, the kind of offence: indictable, under the Taxation Administration Act 1953, or summary
      `the offence is under transport or traffic legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a charge or conviction, whether the offence is under transport or traffic legislation
      `the offence is about parking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a transport or traffic offence, whether it relates to the parking of vehicles
      `the offence is about driving or operating a vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a transport or traffic offence, whether it relates to the driving or operation of vehicles
      `I was sentenced to imprisonment for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a conviction, whether the court sentenced you to a term of imprisonment
      `its maximum imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER @desc For a charge or conviction, the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence, in months (0 if none)
      `a licence disqualification was ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a conviction, whether the court ordered licence disqualification
      `it was drink or drug driving under the NSW or Victorian Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a drink or drug driving offence under the Road Transport Act 2013 (NSW) or the Road Safety Act 1986 (Vic)
GIVETH A `Reporting`
`Must I report this to the Legal Practice Board` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF NOT `I hold a current practising certificate`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `on reporting` (`Must I report this to the Board` `what happened` (`the offence built from` `the offence's class` `the offence is under transport or traffic legislation` `the offence is about parking` `the offence is about driving or operating a vehicle` `I was sentenced to imprisonment for it` `its maximum imprisonment in months` `a licence disqualification was ordered` `it was drink or drug driving under the NSW or Victorian Act`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my written notice to the Board in time (Uniform Law ss 51(1), 88(3)(a): within 7 days)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a current practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a current Australian practising certificate
      `the date it happened` IS A DATE @desc The date of the charge, conviction or other event
      `the date I notify` IS A DATE @desc The date you give the Board written notice
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my notice to the Board in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF NOT `I hold a current practising certificate`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is my notice in time` `the date it happened` `the date I notify`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be ordered to pay for breaching a condition of my practising certificate (Uniform Law s 54), in penalty units?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a current practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a current Australian practising certificate
GIVETH A `Penalty`
`What is the most I can be ordered to pay for breaching a certificate condition` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF NOT `I hold a current practising certificate`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `up to` `What is the most I can be ordered to pay for breaching a condition`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `The client's money (ss 129-145, General Rules rr 42, 52)`

@export Is this money that my firm holds for the client trust money (Uniform Law s 129)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the law practice holds money for the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice (your firm, or the firm acting for you) has received or holds money for the client in the matter
      `what the money is` IS A `What the money is` @desc What the money is, and why the law practice holds it
      `it was received at the client's direction in the ordinary course of legal practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For money for investment, whether it was received in the ordinary course of legal practice and primarily at the client's direction
      `it is invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For money for investment, whether it is invested in the ordinary course of legal practice to maintain or enhance its value until it is paid out
      `the Board has determined it is not trust money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has determined under s 152 that the money is not trust money
      `the Uniform Rules declare it is not trust money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Uniform Rules declare money of this kind not to be trust money
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the client's money trust money` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF NOT `the law practice holds money for the client`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is this money trust money` (`the money built from` `what the money is` `it was received at the client's direction in the ordinary course of legal practice` `it is invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value` `the Board has determined it is not trust money` `the Uniform Rules declare it is not trust money` FALSE FALSE))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my firm warn the client in writing that this money is not trust money and not covered by the fidelity fund (Uniform Law s 134)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the law practice holds money for the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice (your firm, or the firm acting for you) has received or holds money for the client in the matter
      `what the money is` IS A `What the money is` @desc What the money is, and why the law practice holds it
      `it was received at the client's direction in the ordinary course of legal practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For money for investment, whether it was received in the ordinary course of legal practice and primarily at the client's direction
      `it is invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For money for investment, whether it is invested in the ordinary course of legal practice to maintain or enhance its value until it is paid out
      `the Board has determined it is not trust money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has determined under s 152 that the money is not trust money
      `the Uniform Rules declare it is not trust money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Uniform Rules declare money of this kind not to be trust money
      `it pays legal costs due to the law practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the money is for the payment of legal costs already due to the law practice
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my firm warn the client the money is not trust money` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF NOT `the law practice holds money for the client`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must my firm warn the client that this is not trust money` (`the money built from` `what the money is` `it was received at the client's direction in the ordinary course of legal practice` `it is invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value` `the Board has determined it is not trust money` `the Uniform Rules declare it is not trust money` FALSE FALSE) `it pays legal costs due to the law practice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Where must my firm put the client's money (Uniform Law ss 137-143)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the law practice holds money for the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice (your firm, or the firm acting for you) has received or holds money for the client in the matter
      `what the money is` IS A `What the money is` @desc What the money is, and why the law practice holds it
      `it was received at the client's direction in the ordinary course of legal practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For money for investment, whether it was received in the ordinary course of legal practice and primarily at the client's direction
      `it is invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For money for investment, whether it is invested in the ordinary course of legal practice to maintain or enhance its value until it is paid out
      `the Board has determined it is not trust money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has determined under s 152 that the money is not trust money
      `the Uniform Rules declare it is not trust money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Uniform Rules declare money of this kind not to be trust money
      `it was received in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice received the money in cash
      `there is a written direction to deal with it otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client has given a written direction to deal with the money other than by depositing it in the general trust account
GIVETH A `Where it goes`
`Where must my firm put the money` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF NOT `the law practice holds money for the client`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the money goes` (`Where must my firm put the client's money` (`the money built from` `what the money is` `it was received at the client's direction in the ordinary course of legal practice` `it is invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value` `the Board has determined it is not trust money` `the Uniform Rules declare it is not trust money` `it was received in cash` `there is a written direction to deal with it otherwise`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the money in my firm's trust account safe from the firm's creditors and from judgments against the firm or me (Uniform Law s 145)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the law practice holds money for the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice (your firm, or the firm acting for you) has received or holds money for the client in the matter
      `the law practice or an associate is entitled to the money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice or one of its associates (such as one of its lawyers) is itself entitled to the money
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the trust money safe from the firm's creditors` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF NOT `the law practice holds money for the client`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is the trust money safe from my firm's creditors` `the law practice or an associate is entitled to the money`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my firm pay its legal costs out of the client's trust money now (Uniform Law s 144(2)(b), General Rules r 42)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the law practice holds money for the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice (your firm, or the firm acting for you) has received or holds money for the client in the matter
      `a bill referring to the withdrawal was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice gave the client a bill that refers to the proposed withdrawal from trust
      `the day the bill was given` IS A DATE @desc The date the law practice gave the client its bill
      `business days since the bill was given` IS A NUMBER @desc How many business days have passed since the bill was given
      `the client objected within 7 business days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client objected to the withdrawal within 7 business days of the bill
      `the client referred it to the Board or for costs assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client referred the bill to the Board or applied for a costs assessment
      `the client asked for and received an itemised bill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client asked for an itemised bill under s 187 and received it
      `the day the itemised bill was received` IS A DATE @desc The date the client received the itemised bill
      `the money has otherwise become legally payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the money has otherwise become legally payable to the law practice
      `the client's instructions authorise the withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client's written instructions authorise the withdrawal
      `it reimburses money the law practice paid for the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the withdrawal reimburses money the law practice paid on the client's behalf
      `the client was first sent a request for payment or notice of withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client was first sent a request for payment or a notice of the withdrawal
      `the date of the withdrawal` IS A DATE @desc The date of the proposed withdrawal from trust
GIVETH A `Withdrawal`
`May my firm pay its costs out of trust money` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF NOT `the law practice holds money for the client`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `on the withdrawal` (`May my firm take its costs from trust money` (`the withdrawal built from` `a bill referring to the withdrawal was given` `the day the bill was given` `business days since the bill was given` `the client objected within 7 business days` `the client referred it to the Board or for costs assessment` `the client asked for and received an itemised bill` `the day the itemised bill was received` `the money has otherwise become legally payable` `the client's instructions authorise the withdrawal` `it reimburses money the law practice paid for the client` `the client was first sent a request for payment or notice of withdrawal`) `the date of the withdrawal`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my firm give the client a trust account statement now (General Rules r 52)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the law practice holds money for the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice (your firm, or the firm acting for you) has received or holds money for the client in the matter
      `the occasion` IS A `Statement occasion` @desc What has happened: the matter is complete, the client reasonably asked during the matter, or 30 June has passed
      `the ledger has only transit money or written direction money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client's trust ledger records only transit money or money dealt with under a written direction
      `the balance at 30 June was zero` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client's trust ledger balance at 30 June was zero
      `there was no transaction in the 12 months before 30 June` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there was no transaction on the ledger in the 12 months before 30 June
      `a statement was given in those 12 months and there has been no transaction since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a statement was given in those 12 months and there has been no transaction since
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my firm give a trust account statement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF NOT `the law practice holds money for the client`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must my firm give the client a trust account statement` `the occasion` (`the ledger built from` `the ledger has only transit money or written direction money` `the balance at 30 June was zero` `there was no transaction in the 12 months before 30 June` `a statement was given in those 12 months and there has been no transaction since`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Costs disclosure and costs agreements (ss 170, 172(4), 174, 177-179)`

@export Is my client a commercial or government client, so that most of Uniform Law Part 4.3 does not protect it (s 170, General Rules r 71)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the client` IS A `Kind of client` @desc What kind of client the law practice is acting for
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my client a commercial or government client, as a lawyer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        `yes if` (`Is my client a commercial or government client` `the client`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can my client require a negotiated costs agreement with my firm (Uniform Law ss 179, 170)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the client` IS A `Kind of client` @desc What kind of client the law practice is acting for
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my client require a costs agreement, as a lawyer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        `yes if` (`Can my client require a costs agreement` `the client`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What costs disclosure must I give my client at the start of the matter (Uniform Law ss 170, 174, Sch 4 cl 18)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the client` IS A `Kind of client` @desc What kind of client the law practice is acting for
      `likely total legal costs excluding GST and disbursements` IS A NUMBER @desc The total legal costs likely in the matter, in dollars, excluding GST and disbursements
GIVETH A `Disclosure`
`What costs disclosure must I give, as a lawyer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        `disclosure due` (`What costs disclosure must I give` `the client` `likely total legal costs excluding GST and disbursements`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my full costs disclosure meet Uniform Law s 174(1)(a), (2)(a), (3) and (6)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the disclosure was in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the disclosure was in writing
      `it was given when or as soon as practicable after instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was given when, or as soon as practicable after, the law practice was instructed
      `it states the basis on which costs will be calculated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states the basis on which the legal costs will be calculated
      `it estimates the total legal costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it gives an estimate of the total legal costs
      `it states the right to negotiate a costs agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states the client's right to negotiate a costs agreement
      `it states the right to negotiate the billing method` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states the client's right to negotiate the billing method
      `it states the right to a bill and to ask for an itemised bill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states the client's right to receive a bill and to request an itemised bill
      `it states the right to the Board's help in a costs dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states the client's right to seek the Board's assistance in a costs dispute
      `I took reasonable steps to see the client understood and consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you took all reasonable steps to satisfy yourself the client understood and consented
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my costs disclosure meet section 174` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        `yes if` (`Does my disclosure meet section 174` (`My costs disclosure` WITH
            `in writing` IS `the disclosure was in writing`
            `given when or as soon as practicable after instructions` IS `it was given when or as soon as practicable after instructions`
            `states the basis on which costs will be calculated` IS `it states the basis on which costs will be calculated`
            `estimates the total legal costs` IS `it estimates the total legal costs`
            `states the right to negotiate a costs agreement` IS `it states the right to negotiate a costs agreement`
            `states the right to negotiate the billing method` IS `it states the right to negotiate the billing method`
            `states the right to a bill and to ask for an itemised bill` IS `it states the right to a bill and to ask for an itemised bill`
            `states the right to the Board's help in a costs dispute` IS `it states the right to the Board's help in a costs dispute`
            `I took reasonable steps to see the client understood and consented` IS `I took reasonable steps to see the client understood and consented`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I give my client further costs disclosure now (Uniform Law s 174(1)(b), (7), (8))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the disclosure given so far` IS A `Disclosure so far` @desc What costs disclosure the law practice has already given the client
      `likely total legal costs now` IS A NUMBER @desc The total legal costs now likely, in dollars, excluding GST and disbursements
      `a significant change to anything disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anything already disclosed has significantly changed
GIVETH A `Further disclosure`
`Must I give further costs disclosure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        `further disclosure due` (`Must I give further disclosure` `the disclosure given so far` `likely total legal costs now` `a significant change to anything disclosed`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I give my client estimates of the costs payable and contributions expected before a settlement is executed (Uniform Law s 177)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the client` IS A `Kind of client` @desc What kind of client the law practice is acting for
      `it is a litigious matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter involves, or is reasonably likely to involve, proceedings in a court or tribunal
      `the law practice negotiates the settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice negotiates the settlement for the client
      `another law practice that retained it makes the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a law practice that retained this one on the client's behalf makes the disclosure before settlement
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I disclose costs before a settlement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        `yes if` (`Must I disclose costs before settlement` `the client` `it is a litigious matter` `the law practice negotiates the settlement` `another law practice that retained it makes the disclosure`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What follows if my firm did not make the costs disclosure Part 4.3 requires (Uniform Law s 178, General Rules r 72A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the law practice contravened the disclosure obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice failed to make a costs disclosure Part 4.3 requires
      `the decision-maker is satisfied of the r 72A matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board, a costs assessor, a court or a tribunal is satisfied that the law practice took reasonable steps, rectified the failure within 14 days, and the failure was not substantial
GIVETH A `Non-disclosure`
`What follows if my firm did not disclose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        `what follows` (`What follows from not disclosing` `the law practice contravened the disclosure obligations` `the decision-maker is satisfied of the r 72A matters`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my costs agreement prima facie evidence that the costs it discloses are fair and reasonable (Uniform Law s 172(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the disclosure duties were complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Part 4.3 Division 3 (costs disclosure) was complied with
      `the agreement complies with Division 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs agreement neither contravenes nor was made in contravention of Part 4.3 Division 4
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my costs agreement evidence of fair costs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        `yes if` (`Is my costs agreement prima facie evidence of fair costs` `the disclosure duties were complied with` `the agreement complies with Division 4`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Bills, reports, suing and interest (ss 187, 190, 191, 194, 195)`

@export Can my client still ask for an itemised bill (Uniform Law s 187(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the bill given` IS A `The bill given` @desc What bill the law practice has given the client for its legal costs: none yet, a lump sum bill, or an itemised bill
      `the date the costs became payable` IS A DATE @desc The date the legal costs became payable
      `the date of the request for an itemised bill` IS A DATE @desc The date the client asks, or asked, for an itemised bill
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my client still ask for an itemised bill, as a lawyer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF `no lump sum bill has been given` `the bill given`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can my client still ask for an itemised bill` TRUE `the date the costs became payable` `the date of the request for an itemised bill`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my firm's itemised bill in time (Uniform Law s 187(3): within 21 days of the request)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the bill given` IS A `The bill given` @desc What bill the law practice has given the client for its legal costs: none yet, a lump sum bill, or an itemised bill
      `the date of the request for an itemised bill` IS A DATE @desc The date the client asks, or asked, for an itemised bill
      `the date the itemised bill was given` IS A DATE @desc The date the law practice gives, or gave, the itemised bill
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my firm's itemised bill in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF `no lump sum bill has been given` `the bill given`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is our itemised bill in time` `the date of the request for an itemised bill` `the date the itemised bill was given`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much may my firm charge the client for preparing or giving a bill (Uniform Law s 191), in dollars?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much may my firm charge for preparing a bill` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN amount `How much may my firm charge for a bill`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my firm give the client a free written report of costs to date (Uniform Law s 190)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the client` IS A `Kind of client` @desc What kind of client the law practice is acting for
      `the client made a reasonable request for a report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client has reasonably asked for a written report of the legal costs incurred to date
      `another law practice retained this one for the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another law practice retained the law practice on the client's behalf
      `that law practice stopped acting when it did so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that other law practice ceased to act for the client when it retained this one
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my firm give a costs report` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        `yes if` (`Must my firm give a costs progress report` `the client` `the client made a reasonable request for a report` `another law practice retained this one for the client` `that law practice stopped acting when it did so`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- With no bill given, the answer is the baseline's no (s 194(1)), from the bill situation alone.
@export May my firm sue the client for its unpaid legal costs now (Uniform Law ss 178(1)(c), 194, 198(7)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the bill given` IS A `The bill given` @desc What bill the law practice has given the client for its legal costs: none yet, a lump sum bill, or an itemised bill
      `the bill complies with the Law and the Uniform Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the bill complies with the Uniform Law and the Uniform Rules
      `the day the bill was given` IS A DATE @desc The date the law practice gave the client its bill
      `the client asked for and received an itemised bill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client asked for an itemised bill under s 187 and received it
      `the day the itemised bill was received` IS A DATE @desc The date the client received the itemised bill
      `a costs dispute before the Board is unresolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a costs dispute about the bill is before the Board and has not been closed or resolved
      `a costs assessment is applied for and not complete` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a costs assessment has been applied for and is not complete
      `disclosure failed and the costs are not yet assessed or determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice failed to disclose as Part 4.3 requires and the costs have not yet been assessed or the dispute determined
      `the date proceedings would be commenced` IS A DATE @desc The date the law practice would commence proceedings for its costs
GIVETH A `Suing`
`May my firm sue for its unpaid costs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        `on suing` (`May my firm sue for its costs` (`the unpaid bill built from` `the bill given` `the bill complies with the Law and the Uniform Rules` `the day the bill was given` `the client asked for and received an itemised bill` `the day the itemised bill was received` `a costs dispute before the Board is unresolved` `a costs assessment is applied for and not complete` `disclosure failed and the costs are not yet assessed or determined`) `the date proceedings would be commenced`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the highest rate of interest my firm may charge on unpaid legal costs (Uniform Law s 195(4), General Rules r 75), in percent a year?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the bill given` IS A `The bill given` @desc What bill the law practice has given the client for its legal costs: none yet, a lump sum bill, or an itemised bill
      `the Cash Rate Target when the bill was issued` IS A NUMBER @desc The Reserve Bank's Cash Rate Target, in percent, on the date the bill was issued
GIVETH A `Rate`
`What is the highest interest my firm may charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF `no bill has been given` `the bill given`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `at most` (`What is the highest interest rate my firm may charge` `the Cash Rate Target when the bill was issued`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my firm charge this interest on the unpaid legal costs (Uniform Law s 195, General Rules r 75)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the bill given` IS A `The bill given` @desc What bill the law practice has given the client for its legal costs: none yet, a lump sum bill, or an itemised bill
      `a costs agreement provides for interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a costs agreement provides for interest on unpaid costs
      `days the costs have been unpaid since the bill` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days the costs have been unpaid since the bill was given
      `the bill states that interest is payable and the rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the bill states that interest is payable and its rate
      `the rate charged` IS A NUMBER @desc The rate of interest charged, in percent a year
      `the Cash Rate Target when the bill was issued` IS A NUMBER @desc The Reserve Bank's Cash Rate Target, in percent, on the date the bill was issued
      `the bill was given more than 6 months after the matter was completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the bill was given more than 6 months after the matter was completed
      `the lateness came from the client's request or a late itemised bill request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that delay came from the client's request or a late request for an itemised bill
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my firm charge this interest, as a lawyer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF `no bill has been given` `the bill given`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my firm charge this interest` (`the interest claim built from` `a costs agreement provides for interest` `days the costs have been unpaid since the bill` `the bill states that interest is payable and the rate` `the rate charged` `the Cash Rate Target when the bill was issued` `the bill was given more than 6 months after the matter was completed` `the lateness came from the client's request or a late itemised bill request`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Costs assessment and unfair bills (ss 188, 197, 198, 204, 207)`

@export Can my client apply to have my firm's legal costs assessed (Uniform Law ss 170, 197, 198)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the client` IS A `Kind of client` @desc What kind of client the law practice is acting for
      `the date of the bill, request for payment or payment` IS A DATE @desc The date the bill or request for payment was given to the client, or, if neither, the date the costs were paid
      `the date of the application for assessment` IS A DATE @desc The date the client applies, or would apply, for a costs assessment
      `a costs dispute is with the Board and not referred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs are in a costs dispute before the Board that it has neither declared unresolvable nor sent to assessment
      `the designated tribunal has found a late application just and fair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the designated tribunal has determined that it is just and fair to deal with a late application
GIVETH AN `Assessment`
`Can my client have the costs assessed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        `on assessment` (`Can my client have my costs assessed` `the client` `the date of the bill, request for payment or payment` `the date of the application for assessment` `a costs dispute is with the Board and not referred` `the designated tribunal has found a late application just and fair`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Who pays the costs of the costs assessment (Uniform Law s 204)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the costs have been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a costs assessor has assessed the law practice's legal costs in the matter
      `the law practice failed to disclose as Division 3 requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice failed to disclose a matter, or to disclose it in the required manner, under Part 4.3 Division 3
      `the amount billed` IS A NUMBER @desc The legal costs the law practice billed, in dollars
      `the amount assessed` IS A NUMBER @desc The legal costs as assessed, in dollars
      `the assessor finds it unfair for the law practice to pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs assessor believes it is not fair and reasonable in all the circumstances for the law practice to pay
GIVETH AN `Assessment costs`
`Who pays for the assessment, as a lawyer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF NOT `the costs have been assessed`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the assessment costs` (`Who pays for the costs assessment` `the law practice failed to disclose as Division 3 requires` `the amount billed` `the amount assessed` `the assessor finds it unfair for the law practice to pay`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can my firm's charging of more than fair and reasonable costs be a conduct matter against me (Uniform Law ss 188, 207)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the bill given` IS A `The bill given` @desc What bill the law practice has given the client for its legal costs: none yet, a lump sum bill, or an itemised bill
      `the costs were more than fair and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the bill charged more than fair and reasonable legal costs
      `I signed the bill or was nominated as responsible principal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you signed the bill as, or were nominated as, its responsible principal
      `I am a principal and no principal signed or was nominated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a principal of the firm and no principal signed or was nominated for the bill
      `I was involved in giving or authorising the bill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were involved in giving the bill or authorising it to be given
      `I can show I had no reason to suspect the costs were unfair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can establish it was not reasonable for you to suspect or believe the costs were unfair or unreasonable
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can an unfair bill be held against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a lawyer: admitted to the legal profession, practising or about to` THEN
        IF `no bill has been given` `the bill given`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can an unfair bill be a conduct matter against me` `the costs were more than fair and reasonable` `I signed the bill or was nominated as responsible principal` `I am a principal and no principal signed or was nominated` `I was involved in giving or authorising the bill` `I can show I had no reason to suspect the costs were unfair`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the client of a law practice`

§§§ `Who may act for me (ss 6, 150)`

-- s 6 "qualified entity" (a), (d), asked of the person acting for me. The baseline's function is the lawyer's own; the
-- person's facts are passed to it.
@export Is the person acting for me a qualified entity, entitled to engage in legal practice (Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) s 6)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person acting for me is an Australian lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person has been admitted to the Australian legal profession
      `the person acting for me holds a current practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person holds a current Australian practising certificate
      `another law authorises their legal practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a law of the Commonwealth or a State, other than the Uniform Law, authorises the person to engage in legal practice
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the person acting for me a qualified entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        `yes if` (`Am I a qualified entity` `the person acting for me is an Australian lawyer` `the person acting for me holds a current practising certificate` `another law authorises their legal practice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the law practice acting for me receive trust money (Uniform Law s 150, General Rules r 56)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a principal holds a certificate authorising receipt of trust money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a principal (for example a partner) of the law practice holds a practising certificate authorising the receipt of trust money
      `the firm is otherwise authorised under the Uniform Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice is otherwise authorised under the Uniform Rules (General Rules r 56)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the law practice acting for me receive trust money` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        `yes if` (`May my firm receive trust money` `a principal holds a certificate authorising receipt of trust money` `the firm is otherwise authorised under the Uniform Rules`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `My money (ss 129-145, General Rules rr 42, 52)`

@export Is this money my law practice holds for me trust money (Uniform Law s 129)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the law practice holds money for the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice (your firm, or the firm acting for you) has received or holds money for the client in the matter
      `what the money is` IS A `What the money is` @desc What the money is, and why the law practice holds it
      `it was received at the client's direction in the ordinary course of legal practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For money for investment, whether it was received in the ordinary course of legal practice and primarily at the client's direction
      `it is invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For money for investment, whether it is invested in the ordinary course of legal practice to maintain or enhance its value until it is paid out
      `the Board has determined it is not trust money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has determined under s 152 that the money is not trust money
      `the Uniform Rules declare it is not trust money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Uniform Rules declare money of this kind not to be trust money
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my money trust money` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        IF NOT `the law practice holds money for the client`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is this money trust money` (`the money built from` `what the money is` `it was received at the client's direction in the ordinary course of legal practice` `it is invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value` `the Board has determined it is not trust money` `the Uniform Rules declare it is not trust money` FALSE FALSE))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my law practice warn me in writing that this money is not trust money and not covered by the fidelity fund (Uniform Law s 134)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the law practice holds money for the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice (your firm, or the firm acting for you) has received or holds money for the client in the matter
      `what the money is` IS A `What the money is` @desc What the money is, and why the law practice holds it
      `it was received at the client's direction in the ordinary course of legal practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For money for investment, whether it was received in the ordinary course of legal practice and primarily at the client's direction
      `it is invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For money for investment, whether it is invested in the ordinary course of legal practice to maintain or enhance its value until it is paid out
      `the Board has determined it is not trust money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has determined under s 152 that the money is not trust money
      `the Uniform Rules declare it is not trust money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Uniform Rules declare money of this kind not to be trust money
      `it pays legal costs due to the law practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the money is for the payment of legal costs already due to the law practice
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my law practice warn me the money is not trust money` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        IF NOT `the law practice holds money for the client`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must my firm warn the client that this is not trust money` (`the money built from` `what the money is` `it was received at the client's direction in the ordinary course of legal practice` `it is invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value` `the Board has determined it is not trust money` `the Uniform Rules declare it is not trust money` FALSE FALSE) `it pays legal costs due to the law practice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Where must my law practice put my money (Uniform Law ss 137-143)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the law practice holds money for the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice (your firm, or the firm acting for you) has received or holds money for the client in the matter
      `what the money is` IS A `What the money is` @desc What the money is, and why the law practice holds it
      `it was received at the client's direction in the ordinary course of legal practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For money for investment, whether it was received in the ordinary course of legal practice and primarily at the client's direction
      `it is invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For money for investment, whether it is invested in the ordinary course of legal practice to maintain or enhance its value until it is paid out
      `the Board has determined it is not trust money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has determined under s 152 that the money is not trust money
      `the Uniform Rules declare it is not trust money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Uniform Rules declare money of this kind not to be trust money
      `it was received in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice received the money in cash
      `there is a written direction to deal with it otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client has given a written direction to deal with the money other than by depositing it in the general trust account
GIVETH A `Where it goes`
`Where must my law practice put my money` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        IF NOT `the law practice holds money for the client`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the money goes` (`Where must my firm put the client's money` (`the money built from` `what the money is` `it was received at the client's direction in the ordinary course of legal practice` `it is invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value` `the Board has determined it is not trust money` `the Uniform Rules declare it is not trust money` `it was received in cash` `there is a written direction to deal with it otherwise`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my money in the law practice's trust account safe from the law practice's creditors and from judgments against it or its lawyers (Uniform Law s 145)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the law practice holds money for the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice (your firm, or the firm acting for you) has received or holds money for the client in the matter
      `the law practice or an associate is entitled to the money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice or one of its associates (such as one of its lawyers) is itself entitled to the money
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my money safe from the law practice's creditors` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        IF NOT `the law practice holds money for the client`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is the trust money safe from my firm's creditors` `the law practice or an associate is entitled to the money`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my law practice pay its legal costs out of my trust money now (Uniform Law s 144(2)(b), General Rules r 42)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the law practice holds money for the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice (your firm, or the firm acting for you) has received or holds money for the client in the matter
      `a bill referring to the withdrawal was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice gave the client a bill that refers to the proposed withdrawal from trust
      `the day the bill was given` IS A DATE @desc The date the law practice gave the client its bill
      `business days since the bill was given` IS A NUMBER @desc How many business days have passed since the bill was given
      `the client objected within 7 business days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client objected to the withdrawal within 7 business days of the bill
      `the client referred it to the Board or for costs assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client referred the bill to the Board or applied for a costs assessment
      `the client asked for and received an itemised bill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client asked for an itemised bill under s 187 and received it
      `the day the itemised bill was received` IS A DATE @desc The date the client received the itemised bill
      `the money has otherwise become legally payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the money has otherwise become legally payable to the law practice
      `the client's instructions authorise the withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client's written instructions authorise the withdrawal
      `it reimburses money the law practice paid for the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the withdrawal reimburses money the law practice paid on the client's behalf
      `the client was first sent a request for payment or notice of withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client was first sent a request for payment or a notice of the withdrawal
      `the date of the withdrawal` IS A DATE @desc The date of the proposed withdrawal from trust
GIVETH A `Withdrawal`
`May my law practice pay its costs out of my trust money` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        IF NOT `the law practice holds money for the client`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `on the withdrawal` (`May my firm take its costs from trust money` (`the withdrawal built from` `a bill referring to the withdrawal was given` `the day the bill was given` `business days since the bill was given` `the client objected within 7 business days` `the client referred it to the Board or for costs assessment` `the client asked for and received an itemised bill` `the day the itemised bill was received` `the money has otherwise become legally payable` `the client's instructions authorise the withdrawal` `it reimburses money the law practice paid for the client` `the client was first sent a request for payment or notice of withdrawal`) `the date of the withdrawal`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my law practice give me a trust account statement now (General Rules r 52)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the law practice holds money for the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice (your firm, or the firm acting for you) has received or holds money for the client in the matter
      `the occasion` IS A `Statement occasion` @desc What has happened: the matter is complete, the client reasonably asked during the matter, or 30 June has passed
      `the ledger has only transit money or written direction money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client's trust ledger records only transit money or money dealt with under a written direction
      `the balance at 30 June was zero` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client's trust ledger balance at 30 June was zero
      `there was no transaction in the 12 months before 30 June` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there was no transaction on the ledger in the 12 months before 30 June
      `a statement was given in those 12 months and there has been no transaction since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a statement was given in those 12 months and there has been no transaction since
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my law practice give me a trust account statement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        IF NOT `the law practice holds money for the client`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must my firm give the client a trust account statement` `the occasion` (`the ledger built from` `the ledger has only transit money or written direction money` `the balance at 30 June was zero` `there was no transaction in the 12 months before 30 June` `a statement was given in those 12 months and there has been no transaction since`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `What I must be told about costs (ss 170, 174, 177-179)`

@export Am I a commercial or government client, so that most of Uniform Law Part 4.3 does not protect me (s 170, General Rules r 71)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the client` IS A `Kind of client` @desc What kind of client the law practice is acting for
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I a commercial or government client` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        `yes if` (`Is my client a commercial or government client` `the client`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I require my law practice to negotiate a costs agreement with me (Uniform Law ss 179, 170)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the client` IS A `Kind of client` @desc What kind of client the law practice is acting for
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I require a costs agreement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        `yes if` (`Can my client require a costs agreement` `the client`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What costs disclosure must my law practice give me at the start of the matter (Uniform Law ss 170, 174, Sch 4 cl 18)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the client` IS A `Kind of client` @desc What kind of client the law practice is acting for
      `likely total legal costs excluding GST and disbursements` IS A NUMBER @desc The total legal costs likely in the matter, in dollars, excluding GST and disbursements
GIVETH A `Disclosure`
`What costs disclosure must I be given` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        `disclosure due` (`What costs disclosure must I give` `the client` `likely total legal costs excluding GST and disbursements`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my law practice give me further costs disclosure now (Uniform Law s 174(1)(b), (7), (8))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the disclosure given so far` IS A `Disclosure so far` @desc What costs disclosure the law practice has already given the client
      `likely total legal costs now` IS A NUMBER @desc The total legal costs now likely, in dollars, excluding GST and disbursements
      `a significant change to anything disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anything already disclosed has significantly changed
GIVETH A `Further disclosure`
`Must I be given further costs disclosure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        `further disclosure due` (`Must I give further disclosure` `the disclosure given so far` `likely total legal costs now` `a significant change to anything disclosed`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my law practice give me estimates of the costs payable and contributions expected before I execute a settlement (Uniform Law s 177)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the client` IS A `Kind of client` @desc What kind of client the law practice is acting for
      `it is a litigious matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter involves, or is reasonably likely to involve, proceedings in a court or tribunal
      `the law practice negotiates the settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice negotiates the settlement for the client
      `another law practice that retained it makes the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a law practice that retained this one on the client's behalf makes the disclosure before settlement
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I be told the costs before a settlement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        `yes if` (`Must I disclose costs before settlement` `the client` `it is a litigious matter` `the law practice negotiates the settlement` `another law practice that retained it makes the disclosure`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What follows if my law practice did not make the costs disclosure Part 4.3 requires (Uniform Law s 178, General Rules r 72A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the law practice contravened the disclosure obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice failed to make a costs disclosure Part 4.3 requires
      `the decision-maker is satisfied of the r 72A matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board, a costs assessor, a court or a tribunal is satisfied that the law practice took reasonable steps, rectified the failure within 14 days, and the failure was not substantial
GIVETH A `Non-disclosure`
`What follows if my law practice did not disclose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        `what follows` (`What follows from not disclosing` `the law practice contravened the disclosure obligations` `the decision-maker is satisfied of the r 72A matters`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `My bill (ss 187, 190, 191, 194, 195)`

@export Can I still ask my law practice for an itemised bill (Uniform Law s 187(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the bill given` IS A `The bill given` @desc What bill the law practice has given the client for its legal costs: none yet, a lump sum bill, or an itemised bill
      `the date the costs became payable` IS A DATE @desc The date the legal costs became payable
      `the date of the request for an itemised bill` IS A DATE @desc The date the client asks, or asked, for an itemised bill
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I still ask for an itemised bill` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        IF `no lump sum bill has been given` `the bill given`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can my client still ask for an itemised bill` TRUE `the date the costs became payable` `the date of the request for an itemised bill`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 187(3): "The law practice must comply with the request within 21 days after the date on which the request is made".
-- The last day is the 21st day after the request, as the baseline's "Is our itemised bill in time" counts it.
@export By what date must my law practice give me the itemised bill I asked for (Uniform Law s 187(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the bill given` IS A `The bill given` @desc What bill the law practice has given the client for its legal costs: none yet, a lump sum bill, or an itemised bill
      `the date of the request for an itemised bill` IS A DATE @desc The date the client asks, or asked, for an itemised bill
GIVETH A `Date answer`
`By what date must I be given the itemised bill` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        IF `no lump sum bill has been given` `the bill given`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `by` (Date (Day `the date of the request for an itemised bill` PLUS 21))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much can my law practice charge me for preparing or giving a bill (Uniform Law s 191), in dollars?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much can I be charged for a bill` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN amount `How much may my firm charge for a bill`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my law practice give me a free written report of my costs to date (Uniform Law s 190)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the client` IS A `Kind of client` @desc What kind of client the law practice is acting for
      `the client made a reasonable request for a report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client has reasonably asked for a written report of the legal costs incurred to date
      `another law practice retained this one for the client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another law practice retained the law practice on the client's behalf
      `that law practice stopped acting when it did so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that other law practice ceased to act for the client when it retained this one
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I be given a costs report` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        `yes if` (`Must my firm give a costs progress report` `the client` `the client made a reasonable request for a report` `another law practice retained this one for the client` `that law practice stopped acting when it did so`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can my law practice sue me for its unpaid legal costs now (Uniform Law ss 178(1)(c), 194, 198(7)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the bill given` IS A `The bill given` @desc What bill the law practice has given the client for its legal costs: none yet, a lump sum bill, or an itemised bill
      `the bill complies with the Law and the Uniform Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the bill complies with the Uniform Law and the Uniform Rules
      `the day the bill was given` IS A DATE @desc The date the law practice gave the client its bill
      `the client asked for and received an itemised bill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the client asked for an itemised bill under s 187 and received it
      `the day the itemised bill was received` IS A DATE @desc The date the client received the itemised bill
      `a costs dispute before the Board is unresolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a costs dispute about the bill is before the Board and has not been closed or resolved
      `a costs assessment is applied for and not complete` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a costs assessment has been applied for and is not complete
      `disclosure failed and the costs are not yet assessed or determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice failed to disclose as Part 4.3 requires and the costs have not yet been assessed or the dispute determined
      `the date proceedings would be commenced` IS A DATE @desc The date the law practice would commence proceedings for its costs
GIVETH A `Suing`
`Can my law practice sue me now` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        `on suing` (`May my firm sue for its costs` (`the unpaid bill built from` `the bill given` `the bill complies with the Law and the Uniform Rules` `the day the bill was given` `the client asked for and received an itemised bill` `the day the itemised bill was received` `a costs dispute before the Board is unresolved` `a costs assessment is applied for and not complete` `disclosure failed and the costs are not yet assessed or determined`) `the date proceedings would be commenced`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the highest rate of interest my law practice can charge me on unpaid legal costs (Uniform Law s 195(4), General Rules r 75), in percent a year?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the bill given` IS A `The bill given` @desc What bill the law practice has given the client for its legal costs: none yet, a lump sum bill, or an itemised bill
      `the Cash Rate Target when the bill was issued` IS A NUMBER @desc The Reserve Bank's Cash Rate Target, in percent, on the date the bill was issued
GIVETH A `Rate`
`What is the highest interest I can be charged` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        IF `no bill has been given` `the bill given`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `at most` (`What is the highest interest rate my firm may charge` `the Cash Rate Target when the bill was issued`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can my law practice charge me this interest on the unpaid legal costs (Uniform Law s 195, General Rules r 75)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the bill given` IS A `The bill given` @desc What bill the law practice has given the client for its legal costs: none yet, a lump sum bill, or an itemised bill
      `a costs agreement provides for interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a costs agreement provides for interest on unpaid costs
      `days the costs have been unpaid since the bill` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days the costs have been unpaid since the bill was given
      `the bill states that interest is payable and the rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the bill states that interest is payable and its rate
      `the rate charged` IS A NUMBER @desc The rate of interest charged, in percent a year
      `the Cash Rate Target when the bill was issued` IS A NUMBER @desc The Reserve Bank's Cash Rate Target, in percent, on the date the bill was issued
      `the bill was given more than 6 months after the matter was completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the bill was given more than 6 months after the matter was completed
      `the lateness came from the client's request or a late itemised bill request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that delay came from the client's request or a late request for an itemised bill
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be charged this interest` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        IF `no bill has been given` `the bill given`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my firm charge this interest` (`the interest claim built from` `a costs agreement provides for interest` `days the costs have been unpaid since the bill` `the bill states that interest is payable and the rate` `the rate charged` `the Cash Rate Target when the bill was issued` `the bill was given more than 6 months after the matter was completed` `the lateness came from the client's request or a late itemised bill request`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Having my costs assessed (ss 170, 197, 198, 204)`

@export Can I apply to have my law practice's legal costs assessed (Uniform Law ss 170, 197, 198)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the client` IS A `Kind of client` @desc What kind of client the law practice is acting for
      `the date of the bill, request for payment or payment` IS A DATE @desc The date the bill or request for payment was given to the client, or, if neither, the date the costs were paid
      `the date of the application for assessment` IS A DATE @desc The date the client applies, or would apply, for a costs assessment
      `a costs dispute is with the Board and not referred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs are in a costs dispute before the Board that it has neither declared unresolvable nor sent to assessment
      `the designated tribunal has found a late application just and fair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the designated tribunal has determined that it is just and fair to deal with a late application
GIVETH AN `Assessment`
`Can I have my law practice's costs assessed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        `on assessment` (`Can my client have my costs assessed` `the client` `the date of the bill, request for payment or payment` `the date of the application for assessment` `a costs dispute is with the Board and not referred` `the designated tribunal has found a late application just and fair`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 198(3): "within 12 months after (a) the bill was given to, or the request for payment was made to, the client ...; or
-- (b) the legal costs were paid if neither a bill nor a request was made". The last day is counted as the baseline's
-- `months after` counts it (the same day 12 months on, or the month's last day). A commercial or government client has no
-- Part 4.3 assessment (s 170(1), the baseline's finding 7), so for it the question does not arise.
@export By what date must I apply for an assessment of my law practice's legal costs (Uniform Law s 198(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the client` IS A `Kind of client` @desc What kind of client the law practice is acting for
      `the date of the bill, request for payment or payment` IS A DATE @desc The date the bill or request for payment was given to the client, or, if neither, the date the costs were paid
GIVETH A `Date answer`
`By what date must I apply for a costs assessment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        IF `Is my client a commercial or government client` `the client`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `by` (`months after` `the date of the bill, request for payment or payment` 12)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Who pays the costs of the assessment of my law practice's costs (Uniform Law s 204)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the costs have been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a costs assessor has assessed the law practice's legal costs in the matter
      `the law practice failed to disclose as Division 3 requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice failed to disclose a matter, or to disclose it in the required manner, under Part 4.3 Division 3
      `the amount billed` IS A NUMBER @desc The legal costs the law practice billed, in dollars
      `the amount assessed` IS A NUMBER @desc The legal costs as assessed, in dollars
      `the assessor finds it unfair for the law practice to pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs assessor believes it is not fair and reasonable in all the circumstances for the law practice to pay
GIVETH AN `Assessment costs`
`Who pays for the assessment of my costs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the client of a law practice` THEN
        IF NOT `the costs have been assessed`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the assessment costs` (`Who pays for the costs assessment` `the law practice failed to disclose as Division 3 requires` `the amount billed` `the amount assessed` `the assessor finds it unfair for the law practice to pay`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
